NAME
       sendfd, recvfd - pass a descriptor between processes

SYNOPSIS
       int sendfd(int sock, int fd);
       int recvfd(int sock);
       int cervus_sendfd(int sock, int fd);
       int cervus_recvfd(int sock);

DESCRIPTION
       Sends an open descriptor over a Unix domain socket. The receiver
       gets a descriptor of its own referring to the same open file, so
       a process can hand out access to something the other side could
       not have opened itself.

RETURN VALUE
       sendfd returns 0; recvfd returns the new descriptor. Both return
       negative on failure.

ERRORS
       EBADF     the descriptor is not open
       ENOTSOCK  the socket is not a Unix domain socket

SEE ALSO
       socket(2), dup(2), fdpass(1)
